    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (71.92) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.76) serving as our undisputed pillars of production. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a high-floor matchup against Phillips, where his favorable park factor and solid BvP outlook solidify his status as an elite play. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** finds himself in an advantageous spot against Bradish; despite a slight platoon dip, his raw contact quality and the protection provided by the #3 spot in the order keep his expected output firmly in the 70s. **Josh Jung** (62.01) and **Gunnar Henderson** (59.64) are our next most reliable assets, with **Josh Jung** capitalizing on a soft matchup against Pfaadt, where the SP\u2019s 4.49 xERA provides the necessary cushion to boost his base projection significantly.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Coby Mayo**, who landed just shy of the lineup with a score of 38.79. While **Coby Mayo** profiles as a strong power threat, the combination of a tough outing against Miles (3.20 xERA) and the rigid 40.0 efficiency floor dictated by our game-cap management strategy ultimately benched him. Elsewhere, **Heliot Ramos** (59.45) provides a necessary spark; despite the presence of a strong arm behind the plate, his elite sprint speed remains a crucial asset for our stolen base category in today's 5x5 Roto environment. We are monitoring the status of **Henry Bolte** (50.15) closely, as his high-ceiling profile against Woo is bolstered by a +10% park factor, making him a high-variance play that could swing our totals in a favorable direction if he secures base paths early.",
